{
  "$comment": "REQ-TWN-001/005/006 and v1.0 §9. Buildings are authored data: a footprint on the grid, a category, and a tier ladder where each tier states its cost and what it adds to the town.\n\nWhat a building contributes is expressed as capacity and quality, never as a direct bonus to a hunter. Housing and food are counted against population demand (REQ-TWN-003); service points become the service quality that recovery reads (v1.0 §4); job slots are how many people can do a given kind of work at all. A building never touches a hunter's stats — the town changes what the guild can support, and that is what changes hunters.\n\nCosts are authored and reported but not yet charged: the Resources system is Phase 7, and holding half of it here is the temporary architecture §126 forbids. Same treatment as refinement in Phase 2. Tracked in TECH_DEBT.md.\n\n`footprint` is pre-rotation. Build mode rotates in four directions (v1.0 §9), which swaps width and height — so a 3x1 palisade can run along either edge.",
